{"kind":"request","text":"Cross-room send, market slice M0, refiled on a live base\n\nRequest 7542970f now reads stale. It rests on lanes act 0d6d0fba, and that act lost its footing when the M8 landing retired artifacts down its chain. A promise, review request or approval on 7542970f would read stale too. This request carries the same work and rests on nothing, so it stays live. Promise on this request and carry your M0 branch and evidence forward. No step repeats.\n\nThe work is the same as 7542970f:\n1. In a test host, create two rooms with different members. Declare one application with a scope in each room. The receiving scope's genesis names the sending scope.\n2. Send one declared message from the first room's scope to the second's. Show that the receiver admits it.\n3. Show that the receiver refuses the same message from any other sender, with a named refusal.\n4. Show that a reader of the receiving room reads the retained entry and nothing else of the sending room.\n5. Record in an implementation note what today's declared send and admission already do.\n6. Update the roadmap row \"An application's own messages between scopes\" to match what is now true.\n\nRulings 99f628a5 (the delivery contract) and d3f960ab (v1 installation, with the v2 receive-port limit stated in the note and the roadmap) still apply.\n\nDone so far: the corrected v1 witness passes (de331706), and the sender-guard control fails at the named-refusal assertion when the guard is removed (6ea61ce4).\n\nLeft: integrate main 0914c89e, write the note and the roadmap row, run the one gate after S4's, then request review. Landing order: S4, M0, then the formal candidate.","body":{"conditions":"One head on a pushed builder branch that contains main 0914c89e. Tests only for the four cross-room facts. No package or derive source change. One npm run gate before review, in the single validation slot after S4. No live room, deployment or mini access. Builder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","target_head":"0914c89ee94dc61e4df5e9b495a2953eeaad489b","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}